From: Gabriel Duarte Guerra <72227489+GabriWar@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: guard against NULL entries in ttm->pages during unpopulate

amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate() walks ttm->pages[] and writes to
pages[i]->mapping without checking for NULL. If a GPU command fails
partway through, the buffer object can be left partially populated and
the cleanup path then dereferences a NULL page pointer:

  RIP: 0010:amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate+0x77/0xd0 [amdgpu]
  CR2: 0000000000000018
  RAX: 0000000000000000  RBX: ffff8c72d0b6e180  RCX: 0000000000000000
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception

The faulting instruction is the store in the loop:

  48 8b 0b                  mov  (%rbx), %rcx           ; rcx = ttm->pages
  48 8b 0c c1               mov  (%rcx,%rax,8), %rcx    ; rcx = pages[i]
  48 c7 41 10 00 00 00 00   movq $0, 0x10(%rcx)

RCX is 0, and CR2 = 0x18 matches the offset of struct page::mapping,
confirming pages[i] was NULL.

Observed on an AMD BC-250 (gfx1013 / Cyan Skillfish, a PS5-derived APU)
running ROCm compute workloads. GPU command failures on this part are
frequent, and every one of them risked taking the whole machine down:
four hard hangs in a single debugging session, with unclean shutdowns
and filesystem data loss. With this check the failing process still
dies, but the machine survives and the error is recoverable.

Note this addresses the crash, not the underlying reason a buffer object
ends up partially populated, which is a separate issue on this hardware
and is still under investigation. Regardless, unpopulate should not
dereference a NULL page.

Tested on 7.0.12 with a full Stable Diffusion pipeline: output is
unchanged and page faults no longer escalate to kernel panics.

Signed-off-by: Gabriel Duarte Guerra <72227489+GabriWar@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
index 1234567..89abcde 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -1255,8 +1255,9 @@ static void amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate(struct ttm_device *bdev,
 	if (ttm->page_flags & TTM_TT_FLAG_EXTERNAL)
 		return;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ttm->num_pages; ++i)
-		ttm->pages[i]->mapping = NULL;
+	for (i = 0; i < ttm->num_pages; ++i)
+		if (ttm->pages[i])
+			ttm->pages[i]->mapping = NULL;
 
 	adev = amdgpu_ttm_adev(bdev);
 
-- 
2.51.0
